  "paraphrased_text": "The eldest daughter of one of Europe's longest-reigning monarchs, who is also a clairvoyant, married a self-proclaimed sixth-generation shaman from California on Saturday. The wedding of Princess Märtha Louise of Norway to Durek Verrett was anything but a typical royal event, yet crowds gathered along the cloudy streets of Geiranger hoping to see the bride. Princess Märtha Louise, 52, is the only daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja and is fourth in line for the Norwegian throne. She wed Verrett, 49, in a traditional Church of Norway ceremony at the Hotel Union in Geiranger, attended by royals and celebrities. The princess was accompanied by seven bridesmaids, including her teenage daughters Leah and Emma Behn from her previous marriage to the late Ari Behn. Notable guests included Märtha Louise’s brother and his wife, Sweden’s Crown Princess and her husband, and Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien of the Netherlands. Princess Märtha Louise has led an unconventional royal life, having previously identified as a clairvoyant and running a healing school focused on communicating with angels. In 2022, she announced her decision to step back from official royal duties to concentrate on her and Verret’s business ventures. Verret identifies himself on social media as a 'servant of God' and 'energy activator,' with notable clients including Gwyneth Paltrow, whom he refers to as a 'soul sister'."
